# sol vendor_kernel_boot module manifest.
#
# Generated from sol's OWN stock vendor_kernel_boot (AW2A.240903.001.A4): the 98
# modules it actually ships. Do NOT reuse aurora's manifest -- aurora is a different
# board: it lists 51 modules sol does not have, and misses 8 that sol needs
# (sdhci-msm-scaling is a hard dep of sdhci-msm; proxy-consumer, google-extcon-shim,
# touch-nt383x0 = sol's NT383x0 touch controller, etc).
#
# <name>:k  = built by linux-sol      <name>:tp = built by linux-sol-modules
# Tags for names aurora also ships are inherited from its manifest; the sol-only
# ones are classified by origin and MUST be verified against what the build
# actually produces (vkb-assemble's KMI gate will report any that are missing).

arm_smmu:k
bcl_pmic5:k
clk-dummy:k
clk-qcom:k
clk-smd-rpm:k
coresight:k
cpu_hotplug:k
cqhci:k
crypto-qti-common:k
crypto-qti-hwkm:k
dcc_v2:k
debug-regulator:k
dispcc-monaco:k
dwc3-msm:k
eud:k
gcc-monaco:k
gdsc-regulator:k
google-battery:tp
google-bms:tp
google-charger:tp
google-extcon-shim:tp
gpucc-monaco:k
gvotable:tp
hwkm_v1:k
i2c-msm-geni:k
icc-rpm:k
iommu-logger:k
logbuffer:tp
mcu_display:tp
mdt_loader:k
mem_buf:k
mem_buf_dev:k
memory_dump_v2:k
minidump:k
msm_dma_iommu_mapping:k
msm_drm:tp
# Display chain deps. Both are wrong in the inherited stock modules.dep and both
# would fail at boot, verified by unpacking the built vendor_kernel_boot ramdisk
# and comparing modinfo against modules.dep:
#
#   mcu_display really requires nanohub, but its stock dep line is EMPTY, and
#   modules.load is alphabetical so mcu_display (29) loads before nanohub (41).
#   Naked insmod of a module whose supplier is absent is rejected with "Unknown
#   symbol" -- the same failure mode already documented in sol-vkb-assemble.py
#   for sdhci-msm/clk-qcom, which bricked boot at "Waiting for mmcblk0p82".
#
#   msm_drm really requires mcu_display, but the stock line does not mention it,
#   because stock's msm_drm is a different variant. Our build says:
#     depends: qcom_iommu_util,msm_dma_iommu_mapping,mcu_display,spmi-pmic-arb,
#              pinctrl-msm,qcom-scm,panel_event_notifier
#   Alphabetical order happens to put mcu_display first, but that is luck, not a
#   guarantee; modprobe resolves suppliers from modules.dep, so state it.
#
# secure_buffer is kept from the stock line even though our modinfo omits it:
# it is harmless as an extra supplier and stock loads it for this chain.
@dep mcu_display.ko: nanohub.ko
@dep msm_drm.ko: spmi-pmic-arb.ko pinctrl-msm.ko qcom_iommu_util.ko nanohub.ko panel_event_notifier.ko msm_dma_iommu_mapping.ko secure_buffer.ko qcom-scm.ko mcu_display.ko
msm_gpi:k
msm_kgsl:tp
msm_performance:k
msm_sysstats:k
nanohub:tp
nvmem_qcom-spmi-sdam:k
panel_event_notifier:k
phy-generic:k
phy-msm-snps-hs:k
pinctrl-monaco:k
pinctrl-msm:k
pinctrl-spmi-gpio:k
@drop proxy-consumer   # CONFIG_REGULATOR_PROXY_CONSUMER deliberately unset (see sw5100.fragment)
