@drop regmap-spmi   # CONFIG_REGMAP_SPMI=y in our kernel, so no .ko is produced. Stock builds it =m, so the stock modules.dep we inherit lists regmap-spmi.ko as a dependency of qcom-spmi-pmic.ko -- and busybox modprobe resolves modules.dep, fails on the absent file, and ABORTS without loading qcom-spmi-pmic. That left the SPMI bus with no driver at all, so pm5100 was never bound, devm_of_platform_populate() never ran, and none of its children (qcom,qpnp-smblite, pinctrl@8800, rtc@6400, ...) were ever created -- which is why the USB extcon supplier never appeared and adb never came up. The symbols are genuinely built in: Module.symvers shows __devm_regmap_init_spmi_ext exported from vmlinux, not from a module.
rpm-smd:k
rpm-smd-regulator:k
